{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q28209681","formula":"C₂₀H₁₅Cl","hill":"C20H15Cl","elements":["H","C","Cl"],"composition":{"C":20.0,"H":15.0,"Cl":1.0},"names":{"en":"Triphenylchloroethylene"},"descriptions":{"en":"Triphenylchloroethylene (TPCE; brand names Gynosone, Oestrogyl), or triphenylchlorethylene, also known as chlorotriphenylethylene or as phenylstilbene chloride, is a synthetic nonsteroidal estrogen of the triphenylethylene group that was marketed in the 1940s for the treatment of menopausal symptoms, vaginal atrophy, lactation suppression, and all other estrogen-indicated conditions. The estrogenic effects of triphenylethylene, the parent compound of triphenylchloroethylene, were discovered in 1937."},"fame":3,"pubchemCid":87450,"mass":290.8,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=CC=C(C=C1)C(=C(C2=CC=CC=C2)Cl)C3=CC=CC=C3","inchikey":"QEQFTTCZLHLKFX-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"(1-chloro-2,2-diphenylethenyl)benzene","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"87450","atoms":36,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.468,"y":2.903,"z":0.024,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-0.637,"y":0.181,"z":0.002,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.086,"y":0.317,"z":-0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":0.012,"y":-1.169,"z":0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":0.176,"y":1.284,"z":0.008,"el":"C"},{"x":1.648,"y":1.249,"z":0.003,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.783,"y":0.379,"z":1.206,"el":"C"},{"x":0.298,"y":-1.756,"z":-1.208,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.778,"y":0.385,"z":-1.21,"el":"C"},{"x":0.293,"y":-1.76,"z":1.208,"el":"C"},{"x":2.323,"y":1.243,"z":-1.207,"el":"C"},{"x":2.332,"y":1.224,"z":1.208,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.171,"y":0.51,"z":1.204,"el":"C"},{"x":0.903,"y":-3.012,"z":-1.209,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.166,"y":0.515,"z":-1.212,"el":"C"},{"x":0.899,"y":-3.017,"z":1.207,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.863,"y":0.578,"z":-0.006,"el":"C"},{"x":1.204,"y":-3.643,"z":-0.002,"el":"C"},{"x":3.718,"y":1.211,"z":-1.2